WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.300
As 2020 comes to a close, Netflix is finishing
out the year with a brand-new assortment of

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:10.380
television shows, original films, beloved
classics, documentaries, and more to keep

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:12.230
you entertained and occupied.

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:16.939
Here are all the best movies and TV shows
coming to Netflix in December 2020.

00:00:16.939 --> 00:00:22.179
Right at the beginning of the month, Mank,
the newest film from acclaimed director David

00:00:22.179 --> 00:00:24.020
Fincher, arrives on December 4.

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:29.320
Mank tells the story of famed screenwriter
Herman J. Mankiewicz, played by Gary Oldman,

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:32.099
as he writes the classic drama film Citizen
Kane.

00:00:32.099 --> 00:00:37.020
It also details Mankiewicz's personal battles
with director Orson Welles as Citizen Kane

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:40.309
was in production and up to its theatrical
debut in 1941.

00:00:40.309 --> 00:00:43.239
"What is it a writer says?

00:00:43.239 --> 00:00:45.850
Tell the story you know."

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:50.640
With a supporting cast that includes Amanda
Seyfried, Lily Collins, Charles Dance, and

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:55.570
more, as well as a new original score from
frequent Fincher collaborators Trent Reznor

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:59.699
and Atticus Ross, there's no doubt that Mank
will be a movie to watch as awards season

00:00:59.699 --> 00:01:00.699
begins.

00:01:00.699 --> 00:01:05.440
On December 11, musical theater fans will
be able to stream Ryan Murphy's The Prom,

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:08.890
adapted from the award-winning Broadway musical
of the same name.

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:13.760
Featuring megawatt stars like Meryl Streep,
James Corden, and Nicole Kidman, The Prom

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:18.150
centers around Broadway actors longing for
the illustrious days of their past who journey

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:22.690
to a small Indiana town to help a high school
student be allowed to take her girlfriend

00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:23.690
to prom.

00:01:23.690 --> 00:01:28.530
A few days later, on December 18, Chadwick
Boseman's final film will arrive on Netflix.

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:33.210
The world was stunned in August 2020 when
the Black Panther star passed away from stage

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:37.960
IV colon cancer, and his final performance
will come in Ma Rainey's Black Bottom, the

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:42.210
true story of a music legend and one difficult
day in the recording studio.

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:47.340
The film stars Viola Davis as Ma Rainey, an
iconic blues singer, and Boseman co-stars

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:50.440
as the aspirational and determined trumpeter
Levee.

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:55.500
Finally, just before Christmas, George Clooney's
post-apocalyptic thriller The Midnight Sky

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:57.880
will hit Netflix on December 23.

00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:01.910
It tells the tale of a scientist in the Arctic
who's racing against time to stop a group

00:02:01.910 --> 00:02:06.050
of astronauts from returning home to a global
disaster.

00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:10.450
If you're holed up with your family this Christmas
and looking for a new series to binge, Netflix

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:13.030
has no shortage of exciting options.

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:17.201
Netflix will kick off the month with a continuation
of its series The Movies That Made Us, but

00:02:17.201 --> 00:02:19.130
this time, it has a festive twist; Holiday
Movies.

00:02:19.130 --> 00:02:22.430
Holiday Movies That Made Us will hit the service
on December 1.

00:02:22.430 --> 00:02:26.480
Shortly thereafter, the anticipated fourth
season of Nick Kroll's hit animated series

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:31.390
Big Mouth will arrive on December 4, followed
by the premiere of Selena: The Series, which

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:36.870
tells the story of the Tejano singer's life
before a former friend killed her in 1995,

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:39.170
when Selena was just 23 years old.

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:42.790
If you're a fan of thrillers, you'll want
to check out The Mess You Leave Behind, created

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:45.180
by Elite writer Carlos Montero.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:47.630
The series hits Netflix on December 11.

00:02:47.630 --> 00:02:51.510
On the flip side, if you're a music fan looking
for lighter fare, you won't want to miss the

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:57.060
second series of Song Exploder, which interviews
singer-songwriters like Lin-Manuel Miranda

00:02:57.060 --> 00:03:00.590
and Alicia Keys and is based on the podcast
of the same name.

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:03.510
Song Exploder arrives on December 15.

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:07.970
On Christmas Day, Netflix subscribers will
get the best gift of all: Bridgerton, the

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:12.170
first product of showrunner Shonda Rhimes'
huge deal with the streaming service.

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:17.170
Narrated by Dame Julie Andrews as the gossipmonger
Lady Whistledown, Bridgerton follows the ins

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:21.760
and outs of high society in London, and is
sure to draw in fans of Rhimes' previous fare

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:23.810
like Scandal and Grey's Anatomy.

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:28.910
"My name is Lady Whistledown.

00:03:28.910 --> 00:03:31.330
You don't know me and never shall."

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:36.510
Finally, on December 31, just before 2020
comes to an end, you can stream the fourth

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:42.550
and final season of the Kiernan Shipka starring
series Chilling Adventures of Sabrina.

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:46.610
Aside from new original films, Netflix is
adding a ton of beloved classics in December

00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:47.750
2020.

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:51.931
If you're a fan of quirky romantic comedies,
you'll definitely want to check out 50 First

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:56.709
Dates, which stars frequent collaborators
Drew Barrymore and Adam Sandler as a couple

00:03:56.709 --> 00:03:58.590
facing a unique relationship hurdle.

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:02.500
50 First Dates will be available to stream
beginning on December 1.

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:06.520
If you want to relive your childhood with
some of Spielberg's best films, ET the Extra-Terrestrial,

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:11.849
Jurassic Park, and Jurassic Park III will
be available on Netflix as well all hitting

00:04:11.849 --> 00:04:13.870
the streamer on the first of the month.

00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:18.759
Dan Brown enthusiasts will be happy to hear
that both of the author's Tom Hanks-led adaptations,

00:04:18.759 --> 00:04:23.270
The Da Vinci Code and Angels and Demons, will
hit Netflix in December 2020.

00:04:23.270 --> 00:04:27.630
Meanwhile, if you loved Jon Favreau and Roy
Choi's Chef Show, you'll want to check out

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:31.840
Favreau's film Chef, which built the friendship
between Choi and the director.

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:34.139
All of the above hit Netflix on December 1.

00:04:34.139 --> 00:04:38.690
After that, the acclaimed films Nocturnal
Animals and Lee Daniels' The Butler arrive

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:42.129
on Netflix in the middle of the month, on
December 16.

00:04:42.129 --> 00:04:46.759
And just as December draws to a close, you
can revisit the animated flick Rango, which

00:04:46.759 --> 00:04:49.509
arrives on December 28.

00:04:49.509 --> 00:04:54.319
Next month, you can tuck into everything from
a massive reality TV show marathon to a much-beloved

00:04:54.319 --> 00:04:56.949
sci-fi series that's been around forever.

00:04:56.949 --> 00:05:01.870
On December 1, seasons 1 and 2 of the dating
show Are You the One? and seasons 1 and 2

00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:05.099
of tattoo competition Ink Masters will join
Netflix.

00:05:05.099 --> 00:05:10.110
Two weeks later, on December 15, the first
two seasons of Black Ink Crew New York, about

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:14.020
a tattoo shop in Harlem, and seasons 1 and
2 of Teen Mom 2 join the fray.

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:19.530
A couple of seasons of MTV's The Challenge
seasons 10 and 13, specifically will arrive

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:20.699
that same day.

00:05:20.699 --> 00:05:24.659
If you're looking for a gritty new drama to
binge and want to expand your horizons beyond

00:05:24.659 --> 00:05:29.080
the United States, you'll definitely want
to check out season one of Kings of Jo'burg,

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:33.419
a South African drama about the crime world
of Johannesburg that arrives on Netflix on

00:05:33.419 --> 00:05:34.419
December 4.

00:05:34.419 --> 00:05:38.770
And if a tried-and-true series is what you're
after this December, set aside some time to

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:43.949
watch ten seasons of Stargate SG-1, which
hits the platform on the first of the month.

00:05:43.949 --> 00:05:47.659
And those still reeling from the death of
Jeopardy! host Alex Trebek, who passed away

00:05:47.659 --> 00:05:52.840
on November 8, 2020 after battling cancer,
can revisit some of Trebek's best moments

00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:58.740
on December 18 when a slew of Jeopardy challenge
runs and tournaments all arrive on Netflix.

00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:03.211
If you're a fan of hard-hitting documentaries
and or gut-busting stand-up specials, you're

00:06:03.211 --> 00:06:06.349
in for a treat on Netflix in December 2020.

00:06:06.349 --> 00:06:10.139
Those who can't get enough of medical fare
like ER and House will definitely love The

00:06:10.139 --> 00:06:15.759
Surgeon's Cut, which follows real-life surgical
pioneers as they discover new medical breakthroughs.

00:06:15.759 --> 00:06:18.680
The docuseries hits the service on December
9.

00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:20.520
In search of something more uplifting?

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:23.749
Try out Giving Voice, arriving to Netflix
on December 11.

00:06:23.749 --> 00:06:28.099
It tells the true story of the annual August
Wilson monologue competition, which allows

00:06:28.099 --> 00:06:31.639
lucky young winners to perform original works
on Broadway.

00:06:31.639 --> 00:06:36.009
True crime buffs, however, will want to free
up their schedules on December 16, as that's

00:06:36.009 --> 00:06:37.990
when The Ripper drops on Netflix.

00:06:37.990 --> 00:06:42.900
The documentary follows real-life witnesses
and investigators as they recall how the Yorkshire

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:46.919
Ripper, described as "a modern-day Jack the
Ripper," tormented northern England in the

00:06:46.919 --> 00:06:47.990
late '70s.

00:06:47.990 --> 00:06:52.560
Meanwhile, Netflix will also give a voice
to some fresh new faces in stand-up comedy.

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:57.770
On December 1, Natalie Palamides will make
her Netflix debut with Nate - A One Man Show,

00:06:57.770 --> 00:07:00.369
where she uses an alter-ego for her stand-up.

00:07:00.369 --> 00:07:05.319
The very next day, on December 2, Ari Eldjarn
and Hazel Brugger also step into the world

00:07:05.319 --> 00:07:10.409
of Netflix original specials with the premieres
of their respective specials Pardon My Icelandic

00:07:10.409 --> 00:07:11.409
and Tropical.

00:07:11.409 --> 00:07:16.499
And finally, if you're looking to celebrate
New Year's Eve with some laughs, load up Netflix's

00:07:16.499 --> 00:07:21.970
Best Stand-Up of 2020 - a compilation of "the
funniest jokes from comedians in the US, Canada,

00:07:21.970 --> 00:07:26.710
Australia and New Zealand that have launched
specials in 2020."

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:28.599
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:07:28.599 --> 00:07:32.490
Plus, even more Looper videos about what to
watch on your favorite streaming platforms

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:34.089
are coming soon.

00:07:34.089 --> 00:07:37.509
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

